#
#	OpenTPW umbrellas: the brolly shop (modelled on the keys of the original balloon shop, a shop)
#	Every number marked "OpenTPW's own value" is a choice of this extension. The values that come from the Theme Park Inc brolly shops
#	(price 30, goods 10 to 15, happiness 20, litter 10 to 20, rain and storm 200 %, snow 150 %, heat wave 5 %; docs/UMBRELLAS.md) are marked "as Theme Park Inc".
#	The kid score is 75 %: it follows Theme Park Inc's value, per the owner's decision.
#
Info.Id			64500		placeholder: objects.json replaces it with the object's own id
Info.Name		"Brolly Shop"
Info.IsChoosable	1
Info.HasQueue		0		a shop: guests walk to it and buy, no queue
Info.WhichUIType	1		a shop (the build menu's Shops tab)

# A 2 x 2 booth. The entrance '2' (where the customer stands, facing the counter) is the lower left cell.
Info.Shape
---
**
2*
---

# The construction fence for 2 x 2 cells: the four corner pieces
Info.Hoarding
---
F7
LJ
---

# 1 = a gift shop's kind (the closest of the original shop kinds; OpenTPW's own value)
UsageInfo.ShopType			1
UsageInfo.InitCostOfGoods		13		as Theme Park Inc (10 to 15)
UsageInfo.InitPricePerUse		30		as Theme Park Inc
UsageInfo.EntryCellStandPosX	0.5
UsageInfo.EntryCellStandPosY	0.5
UsageInfo.ExitCellAppearPosX	0.5
UsageInfo.ExitCellAppearPosY	0.5
UsageInfo.RideHandlesSprite	1		the shop's script hides the customer while serving (as the balloon shop)
UsageInfo.MinCapacity		0		always zero for shops
UsageInfo.MaxCapacity		0		always zero for shops

# Not indoors: the umbrella's own weather percentages below are what makes guests seek it in the rain, so the original's indoor-in-rain bonus must not stack on them
UsageInfo.ISIndoors			0

UsageInfo.ThirstEffect		0
UsageInfo.HungerEffect		0
UsageInfo.VomitEffect		0
UsageInfo.HappinessEffect		20		as Theme Park Inc
UsageInfo.LitterEffect		15		as Theme Park Inc (10 to 20)

# 3 = the guest gets an open umbrella (1 balloon and 2 costume are the original's; 3 is Theme Park Inc's and this extension's)
UsageInfo.AppearanceEffect		3

# Weather and generation multipliers (Theme Park Inc's keys; the original does not read them, the umbrellas extension reads them for its own objects only), percent of the attraction score
WeatherModifier.RainPercentage		200		as Theme Park Inc
WeatherModifier.StormPercentage	200		as Theme Park Inc
WeatherModifier.SnowPercentage		150		as Theme Park Inc
WeatherModifier.HeatWavePercentage	5		as Theme Park Inc; Theme Park World has no heat wave
GenerationModifier.KidScorePercentage	75		follows Theme Park Inc's value, per the owner's decision

Research.Group		0		available from the start, no research
Info.PreviewAnimNum		0

Upgrades[0].InitCapacity		10		as Theme Park Inc (5 or 10)
Upgrades[0].CostOfUpgrade		1000		OpenTPW's own value
Upgrades[0].CostOfResearch		0		An object without research cost starts researched
Upgrades[0].RunningCost		35		OpenTPW's own value (a Theme Park Inc key; the original does not read it)
